course: dictionary
lesson: 1656
title: A word from nature
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chipmunk is a small striped squirrel, and the sentence it appears in gives you a clue. «The squirrel family alone holds tree squirrels, flying squirrels, chipmunks, marmots and prairie dogs, which are really ground squirrels that bark.» Chipmunks are listed with other squirrels, so a chipmunk must belong to the squirrel family.
explain: Lists are a useful context clue. Words in a list often belong to the same group. Tree squirrels, flying squirrels and chipmunks are all squirrels, and the list also names marmots and prairie dogs. You do not need to know exactly what a marmot is to see that they belong together.
explain: Look at the word «really» in the same sentence. Prairie dogs have a dog-like name, but «really» tells you they are a kind of squirrel. When a name seems to suggest one thing, check the rest of the sentence before you decide.
fact: A chipmunk is a small striped squirrel that lives in North America, with one kind found in Asia.
fact: Chipmunks live in burrows, which are holes dug in the ground.
fact: Chipmunks carry food in their cheek pouches, so their cheeks puff out. This is why people say «chipmunk cheeks».
fact: Many chipmunks store nuts for winter.
fact: In stories and cartoons, such as Alvin and the Chipmunks, chipmunks are cheeky and fast.
exercise: «The squirrel family alone holds tree squirrels, flying squirrels, chipmunks, marmots and prairie dogs.» Which group does a chipmunk belong to? | Dogs | Fish | *Squirrels | Birds
exercise: Ella says, «She has chipmunk cheeks after lunch.» What does chipmunk cheeks mean? | *Puffed-out cheeks | Cold cheeks in winter | Very red cheeks | Thin, flat cheeks
exercise: Where do chipmunks live? | *In burrows, which are holes in the ground | On the roofs of houses | Up in the clouds | In the sea
test: How does a chipmunk carry its food? | In its tail | In a bag on its back | *In its cheek pouches | In its ears
test: In the sentence «prairie dogs, which are really ground squirrels that bark», what does «really» tell you? | *That the name may mislead: they are a kind of squirrel | That the sentence is a joke | That they cannot bark | That they are dogs
exam: Using «The squirrel family alone holds tree squirrels, flying squirrels, chipmunks, marmots and prairie dogs», what is a chipmunk? | A kind of bird that flies | A large dog that barks | A fish that lives in the sea | *A small striped squirrel
